To automatically tag unlabeled IPv4 prefixes learned from external neighbors with the link-bandwidth attribute for inbound traffic engineering, use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group <EBGP_Group_Name>
        link-bandwidth
            add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
```

**Key details:**
- Apply this under the BGP group containing directly connected EBGP peers.
- The `add-to-received-ebgp ipv4` command automatically adds the link-bandwidth extended community to unlabeled IPv4 routes received from single-hop EBGP peers.
- The link-bandwidth value is derived from the circuit capacity of the peering interface.

For neighbor-specific configuration (if required):
```cli
configure router bgp
    group <EBGP_Group_Name>
        neighbor <Peer_IP>
            link-bandwidth
                add-to-received-ebgp ipv4
```

