To ensure BGP session stability during transient link failures on Nokia 7750 SR routers, enable BGP Graceful Restart with adjusted timers to preserve neighbor relationships during brief interface flaps. Use the following configuration:

```cli
configure router bgp
    graceful-restart
        restart-time 120
        stale-routes-time 300
    exit
```

### Key Details:
- **`graceful-restart`**  
  Enables BGP to maintain sessions and retain routes during peer restarts (default: disabled).

- **`restart-time 120`**  
  Advertises a 120-second recovery window to neighbors (default: 120 globally). This gives the router time to re-establish sessions after transient failures.

- **`stale-routes-time 300`**  
  Extends stale route retention to 300 seconds (default: none), ensuring continuous forwarding during instability.

Apply this globally under BGP configuration to cover all peers. For peer-specific adjustments, use the same commands within `group` or `neighbor` contexts. This setup prevents immediate session resets during OSPF flaps by leveraging BGP's error-recovery mechanisms.
