**Explanation:**  
This configuration enables link-bandwidth processing for BGP routes received from EBGP neighbors. The `aggregate-used-paths ipv4` command sums the bandwidth values from link-bandwidth extended communities of all active multipaths (ECMP routes) for IPv4 prefixes. When readvertising these routes with `next-hop-self`, the router attaches the aggregated bandwidth value to the route, allowing downstream devices to utilize the total available bandwidth of the logical bundle.  

**Key points:**  
- Applied at the BGP group level (e.g., `ebgp-peers`) where external peers are configured  
- Operates on unlabeled IPv4 unicast routes (`ipv4` family)  
- Only aggregates bandwidth from *used* ECMP paths (active forwarding paths)  
- Automatically processes incoming link-bandwidth extended communities from EBGP peers  

**Verification:**  
After implementation, check routes with `show router bgp routes <prefix> detail` to confirm the presence of the aggregated link-bandwidth extended community value.
