To ensure consistent path selection by dynamically setting the MED attribute based on IGP metrics when peering with Cisco devices, use the `med-out igp-cost` command. Apply this configuration to the relevant BGP group or neighbor:

**For a specific BGP group:**
```
configure router bgp
    group "Cisco-Peers"
        med-out igp-cost
    exit
exit
```

**For a specific neighbor:**
```
configure router bgp
    group "Cisco-Peers"
        neighbor 192.0.2.1
            med-out igp-cost
        exit
    exit
exit
```

