To ensure uninterrupted BGP routing during controlled reboots of your Nokia 7750 SR routers, configure Long-Lived Graceful Restart (LLGR) helper functionality for your core BGP peers. Use the following CLI commands to enable LLGR and set appropriate timers:

```cli
configure router bgp
    group "CORE"
        graceful-restart
            restart-time 300
            long-lived
                stale-routes-time 1800
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Key Details:**  
- `graceful-restart` activates helper functionality for supported address families.  
- `restart-time 300` sets the maximum expected peer recovery time (default: 300 seconds).  
- `long-lived` enables extended route preservation during outages.  
- `stale-routes-time 1800` retains stale routes for 1800 seconds (30 minutes) during peer reboots.  

**Apply to Specific Peers:**  
If configuring individual neighbors instead of a group:  
```cli
configure router bgp
    neighbor <IP>
        graceful-restart
            long-lived
                stale-routes-time 1800
            exit
        exit
    exit
exit
```

**Verification:**  
After configuration, confirm with:  
```cli
show router bgp group "CORE" detail  
show router bgp neighbor <IP> capabilities
```  

**Note:** Ensure all core BGP peers support LLGR capabilities. Adjust `stale-routes-time` based on your maintenance window duration (valid range: 1–3600 seconds).
